# Backups are encrypted to these age public keys (one per line). backup.sh passes this file to
# `age -R`, so an empty or missing file means every nightly dump fails to encrypt.
#
# Generate the pair on a machine that is NOT this host:
#
#   age-keygen -o rm-backup-identity.key
#
# The command prints the public key; put it here. The private key is what restores a backup, so
# it must live somewhere the restore drill can reach it and nowhere a compromise of this host
# would — if both sit on the VPS, encrypting the backups protects against nothing.
#
# age1................................................................
